# The Nameless Inversion ruling: "If a creature loses all creature types but then gains a new creature type later in the
# turn, it will be that new creature type." Bot1's Concealing Curtains, a 0/4 Wall, loses all creature types to the
# Inversion, then Scale Up makes it a green Wurm with base power and toughness 6/4. Layer 4 applies in timestamp order
# (CR 613.7), so the later Wurm stays: it is a Wurm, 9/1 with the Inversion's +3/-3 on top of the new base (CR 613.4b-c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Concealing Curtains
Nameless Inversion
Scale Up
Swamp x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Concealing Curtains.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Nameless Inversion.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Subtypes = (absent)
Bot1.Hand.Scale Up.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Subtypes = Wurm
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Power = 9
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Toughness = 1
